  "body": "## Why\nThe eleven courses following Sonnenhafen were substantially shorter, with several passages consisting of open arches or repeated short boxes. Rivals shared much of their facial geometry, the rabbit's eyes protruded, and held items differed mainly by color. Gate animation also rotated the road-aligned placement root.\n\n## Changes\n- Author eleven distinct 1.96–2.04 km routes, retaining Sonnenhafen's existing 1,851.68 m curve.\n- Connect continuous themed passages with actual 11.6–14.3 m descents, suitable outer cover, reserved action spans and expanded roadside scenery.\n- Refine four rival species, rabbit eye seating and all fourteen chassis while preserving mechanical anchors and original imported Lumo assets.\n- Add a genuine, validated rival GLB adapter. All currently pending roster models remain disabled.\n- Add solid wind/shield/pulse emblems, universal skill-gate crowns and a single race-owned FX clock with pause and reduced-motion handling.\n- Add reproducible Godot geometry reviews and GLB-to-Blender exports. See [handoff and validation](https://github.com/Ullmann27/lumo-godot/blob/c84926650363c2faab8a83ee592ebd7aa8486a6d/docs/design/2026-11-14-kart-adventure/README.md).\n- Preserve sRGB vertex palettes and linear emissive factors in Blender exports, including instance material overrides. Keep binary geometry unchanged during emission correction and retain strict integer JSON fields.\n- Export tunnel MultiMeshes through an actual renderer; reject dummy-backend readback, retain all road ribbons, verify copied transforms/materials and reuse identical tint materials. Match the reviewed banked camera and document the studio-only lights and albedo-guided CPU noise filter.\n\n## Local validation\n- 12/12 curve contracts; 11/11 complete world builds at low detail, plus every new tunnel at both geometry levels.\n- 24 physical laps, 192 ordered checkpoints, zero resets across all 12 tracks. The first ten per-course results precede a process termination; Desert and Lab passed in a fresh process.\n- Six actual interior raster views plus six hidden-shell negative controls, with backface culling enabled.\n- All 14 chassis detail/contact gates; 16,280 procedural steering measurements.\n- Original imported Lumo: 1,196 cadence/contact/pause checks.\n- Rival adapter: 46 checks, including repeated actual vehicle state calls at 60/144 Hz.\n- Item award/use/save continuity, actual-island FX timing/pause, and at least 0.143 m rabbit attachment clearance.\n- Actual runtime item, vehicle and tunnel GLBs exported and re-imported successfully. Final tunnel export verifies all 576 themed instances against runtime transforms and material values, retaining 2,595 nearby road instances and nine road ribbons. The eight accepted vehicle/item files remain byte-identical after the tunnel fixes; all three export manifests share the final source hashes.\n- Blender 4.3.2/Cycles has produced actual vehicle and item stills and a 48-frame item loop. MP4 and GIF each contain four seconds at 960 × 540; these are studio model previews, not live race captures.\n\n## Review limits\nThis remains a draft. Large complete-world/software-GL action captures ended with external signal 9 and are not accepted as full renderer validation. Bounded product geometry reviews passed. Physical Android GPU/FPS and a newly installed APK have not been verified. Near rival geometry increases approximately 9–11%; distant proxies omit the new wheel microdetails.\n\nThis branch is isolated from the integration branch and main. Tests ran locally; the commit carries `[skip ci]`.",
